## Executive Summary

Claude Opus 4.8 is Anthropic's flagship reasoning model from their Claude family, released May 28, 2026, designed for complex, long-horizon agentic workflows, coding, and professional knowledge work. It features a massive 1M token context window, competitive pricing ($5/$25 per 1M tokens), and exceptional performance on mathematical reasoning benchmarks (96.7% on USAMO 2026, 80.0% on FrontierMath v2 Tiers 1-3). The model leads on most evaluations except Terminal-Bench 2.1, where OpenAI's GPT-5.5 holds the top spot. Opus 4.8 is positioned as a "modest but tangible improvement" over Opus 4.7, with significant gains in honesty (4x less likely to allow flaws in code to pass unremarked) and agentic capabilities. Opus 4.8 was replaced by Claude Opus 5 on July 24, 2026, which offers similar pricing but improved performance across all benchmarks.

---

## Model Identity and Background

**Developer:** Anthropic
**Release Date:** May 28, 2026
**Series:** Claude Opus (Opus 4.6, 4.7, 4.8, 5, 5.5)
**Predecessor:** Claude Opus 4.7 (April 16, 2026)
**Successor:** Claude Opus 5 (July 24, 2026)
**License:** Proprietary
**Context Window:** 1,000,000 tokens
**Max Output:** 128,000 tokens

Claude Opus 4.8 is Anthropic's flagship reasoning model from their Claude family, released May 28, 2026. It was released as a "modest but tangible improvement" over Opus 4.7, with significant gains in honesty (4x less likely to allow flaws in code to pass unremarked) and agentic capabilities. The model was replaced by Claude Opus 5 on July 24, 2026, which offers similar pricing ($5/$25 per 1M tokens) but improved performance across all benchmarks. Opus 4.8 was the highest-ranked Claude model until Fable 5 (launched June 9, 2026) was released, which occupies the new Mythos tier above Opus.

