### Best For:
- Complex, long-horizon agentic workflows (multi-hour coding sessions)
- Software engineering and software development
- Enterprise applications requiring strong reasoning capabilities
- Organizations heavily invested in Anthropic ecosystem
- Cost-sensitive applications with good prompt caching strategies
- Multimodal applications requiring vision capabilities
- Organizations seeking frontier-level performance
- Research-grade tasks requiring strong mathematical reasoning

### Not Ideal For:
- Cost-sensitive applications without prompt caching (Claude Sonnet 5 is 2.5x cheaper)
- Organizations outside Anthropic ecosystem
- Applications requiring frontier-level performance (Claude Opus 5 is more capable)
- Organizations with strict data sovereignty requirements
- Real-time applications requiring ultra-low latency
- General-purpose applications (Claude Sonnet 5 offers comparable performance at 2.5x lower cost)

